```

Output

```text
Umangi Patel
```

---

# 5️⃣ String Traversal

Traversal means visiting every character of a string.

---

### Example

```cpp
#include<iostream>
using namespace std;

int main()
{
    string str = "Hello";

    for(int i=0;i<str.length();i++)
    {
        cout<<str[i]<<" ";
    }
}
```

Output

```text
H e l l o
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(n)
```

---

# 6️⃣ Common String Functions

## length()

Returns the total number of characters.

```cpp
string str = "Coding";

cout<<str.length();
```

Output

```
6
```

---

## size()

Works exactly like `length()`.

```cpp
cout<<str.size();
```

Output

```
6
```

---

## empty()

Checks whether the string is empty.

```cpp
string str = "";

cout<<str.empty();
```

Output

```
1
```

---

## clear()

Removes every character.

```cpp
string str = "Hello";

str.clear();
```

Output

```
""
```

---

# 7️⃣ Access Characters

Characters can be accessed using their index.

```cpp
string str = "Apple";

cout<<str[0];
```

Output

```
A
```

---

### Last Character

```cpp
cout<<str[str.length()-1];
```

Output

```
e
```

---

# 8️⃣ String Comparison

Two strings can be compared using `==`.

```cpp
string a = "Hello";

string b = "Hello";

if(a==b)

cout<<"Equal";
```

Output

```
Equal
```

---

# 9️⃣ String Concatenation

Concatenation means joining two strings.

```cpp
string first = "Hello";

string second = "World";

cout<<first + " " + second;
```

Output

```
Hello World
```

---

# 🔟 Character Functions

```cpp
toupper(ch)
```

Converts character into uppercase.

Example

```
a → A
```

---

```cpp
tolower(ch)
```

Converts character into lowercase.

Example

```
A → a
```

---

```cpp
isdigit(ch)
```

Checks whether a character is a digit.

---

```cpp
isalpha(ch)
```

Checks whether a character is an alphabet.

---

# 📊 Complexity Summary

| Operation | Time Complexity |
|-----------|-----------------|
| Access Character | O(1) |
| Traverse String | O(n) |
| length() | O(1) |
| size() | O(1) |
| Comparison | O(n) |
| Concatenation | O(n) |

