# 💡 Interview Tips

✅ A string is essentially a character array with additional built-in functions.

✅ `getline()` is preferred when input contains spaces.

✅ `length()` and `size()` return the same value.

✅ Characters are accessed using indexing like arrays.

✅ String comparison is case-sensitive.

---

# 📝 Summary

- Strings store sequences of characters.
- Use `getline()` to read complete sentences.
- Traverse strings using loops.
- Built-in functions simplify string operations.
- Understanding string basics is essential before solving interview problems.

